  pages={2431-2441},
  abstract={This work presents the first hybrid crypto system-on-chip (SoC) for secure neural interfacing based on post-quantum cryptography (PQC) and lightweight cryptography (LWC). The transmitted signals are protected through a two-stage hybrid cryptosystem, in which handshake and data encryption are protected by PQC and LWC, respectively. Algorithms are well explored for PQC and LWC, including Falcon digital signature algorithm (DSA), NTRU key encapsulation mechanism (KEM), and ASCON authenticated encryption (AE). Hardware cost is minimized through algorithm-architecture optimizations, including serial-based number theoretic transform (NTT), integrated polynomial multiplication, MK modular multiplication, and shuffling-based fixed-type polynomial sampling. Fabricated in 40-nm CMOS, the SoC integrates 921 K logic gates in core area of 0.62 mm2. The chip supports post-quantum secure neural interfacing for various data formats. The power consumption is 4.8 mW at 50 MHz from a 0.7 V supply. This chip consumes  $0.7~\mu $ J/OP and 48 pJ/B for the PQC handshake and LWC data encryption, respectively. Compared to the state-of-the-art designs, the SoC dissipates 12-to- $46\times $  less energy and achieves 1.3-to- $168\times $  higher area efficiency for the handshake, and dissipates  $7\times $  less energy and achieves  $3\times $  higher area efficiency for data encryption.},
